  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved only ~48.5% accuracy, a weak baseline. The most critical uncertainty at this stage is whether the image modality is more informative than RNA for this task, since all remaining experiments (multimodal fusion, better encoders) depend on knowing which modality carries signal. Question: Does image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) outperform or underperform the RNA-only baseline? This is the cleanest modality comparison—same profile setting (singleprofile), no confounding aggregation or fusion—so any accuracy difference isolates the modality effect. Why this is the best next experiment: With 8 experiments left, establishing whether image features are competitive or superior to RNA features will determine whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion configs or in improving single-modality representations (better encoders, multiprofile). Testing a multimodal config now would confound modality contribution with fusion strategy, making it harder to interpret results."
}

